nd input shapes. Do not assume that another tedi or an operator exposes the same namespaces. Batch dependent reads and writes in one Code Mode program and return a compact result. If a capability is unavailable, report the missing capability and stop that operation; never invent a callable or retry unchanged arguments.\n\nRecord the cycle''s actual outcome through the discovered rationale capability when available. Supply your real tedi and organization identity and the current runId, workItemId, or toolCallRefs required by its schema. Use a schema-supported category and evidence shape; do not fabricate an execution link. Record failure or partial completion honestly, and claim success only for verified effects.\n\nWeekly growth snapshot:\n1. Discover cognitive health and scheduled-cycle health reads for your real tedi identity.\n2. Review bounded memory, skill, muscle-memory, rationale, and tool-execution metrics against the previous snapshot.\n3. For a verified regression, inspect existing Work Items before proposing a bounded follow-up through the Work factory; preserve its admission and review requirements.\n4. Record the measured snapshot and actual outcome so the Growth Timeline stays current."}]')
), retired AS (
  SELECT owner.id, item.key
  FROM tedis AS owner,
    json_each(CASE WHEN json_valid(owner.runtime_overrides) THEN owner.runtime_overrides ELSE '{}' END,
      '$.cronPolicy.cronTemplates') AS item
  WHERE item.type = 'object' AND EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM defaults
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (
      SELECT fullkey, type, atom FROM json_tree(item.value)
      EXCEPT SELECT fullkey, type, atom FROM json_tree(defaults.value)
    ) AND NOT EXISTS (
      SELECT fullkey, type, atom FROM json_tree(defaults.value)
      EXCEPT SELECT fullkey, type, atom FROM json_tree(item.value)
    )
  )
)
UPDATE tedis AS owner
SET runtime_overrides = json_set(owner.runtime_overrides, '$.cronPolicy.cronTemplates', json((
  SELECT json_group_array(json(kept.value))
  FROM (
    SELECT owner.runtime_overrides -> ('$.cronPolicy.cronTemplates[' || item.key || ']') AS value
    FROM json_each(owner.runtime_overrides, '$.cronPolicy.cronTemplates') AS item
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM retired WHERE retired.id = owner.id AND retired.key = item.key
    )
    ORDER BY CAST(item.key AS INTEGER)
  ) AS kept
)))
WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM retired)
  AND json_type(runtime_overrides, '$.cronPolicy.cronTemplates') = 'array';
